   "mask": [
    "\"id\" : \"[^\"]*\"",
    "\"created\" ?: ?\\d+",
    "chatcmpl-[A-Za-z0-9]+"
   ]
  },
  {
   "tcp": [
    {
     "text": "CONNECT mocked.example.test:80 HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: mocked.example.test:80\r\n\r\n"
    },
    {
     "text": "POST /v1/chat/completions HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: mocked.example.test:80\r\nContent-Type: application/json\r\nContent-Length: 95\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n{\"model\": \"gpt-4o\", \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"I want my money back, order 4\"}]}"
    }
   ],
   "chunkMillis": 1000,
   "awaitBytes": 129,
   "minMillis": 2000,
   "text": true,
   "mask": [
    "\"id\" : \"[^\"]*\"",
    "\"created\" ?: ?\\d+",
    "chatcmpl-[A-Za-z0-9]+",
    "\"created_at\" ?: ?\\d+"
   ],
   "note": "a cleartext CONNECT tunnel, eighth registration: RelayConnectHandler's loopback client is on the proxy client's event loop (no turn taken), but the loopback connection it opens is accepted, the next registration on the worker group, on the pooled channel's loop: the tunnelled request is handled there and its verdict times out"
  },
  {
   "sleepMillis": 1500,
   "note": "the tunnelled verdict stalled: its request is written to the pooled connection only once the loop is free, and the next call reuses that connection only after the write and its answer are done, or opens another one: a registration the steps below count"
  },
  {
   "method": "POST",
